[Music]  lgbtiq  rights in the european union are at a  defining moment  most europeans regardless of their  sexuality or gender  want to embrace lgbtiq people as full  members of our european family  they want an end to exclusion  discrimination and violence  but there are forces among us that want  to undo  what is being achieved we must keep  sight of the lgbtiq freedom zone  that we are building on the occasion of  world pride in copenhagen  let us remind everyone that lgbtiq  rights are human rights  these include marching in the streets as  visible members of the lgbtiq community  loving who you want to love and being  who you  truly are through a sense of a global  community  world pride sends a strong signal to the  whole world  that love wins over hate pride raises  awareness of current lgbt iq equality  issues  and the challenges for lgbtiq people  to be themselves and live their lives as  is right for them  pride stands by everyone's uniqueness as  full citizens of societies  with equal rights and obligations pride  is a political protest that keeps up the  pressure for  change combating inequality stereotypes  and structural discrimination pride is  about our shared humanity  we all want to live life to the fullest  be true to ourselves  and express that without fear the  european union  will do its utmost to build a world of  equality  where the rights and freedoms enshrined  in international treaties  apply to all without exception happy  [Music]  pride

